{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass on this day.</b> It was a day like the rest of the days. For the praise of the righteous one and the disgrace of the accursed one this verse was written, for it is not customary to have relations by day. Therefore it is obvious that his intention was nothing but to do his work, and she — even so — <b>ותתפשהו בבגדו</b> (seized him by his garment). Rabbi Yishmael says: it was the day of the Nile's rising, and everyone had gone to see, for such was the custom — when the Nile rises, the king and the ministers go to see and rejoice at the river, and she and he did not go." "<b>And he came into the house.</b> Even if he came only from outside, it says <b>ויבא</b> (and he came)."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:02.050428306Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}